## Gaps

The operator spreadsheet begins 2013-08-17, so none of this year comes from it.

All 342 rows are from the live X walk, taken in batches of ten, and the page

will be appended as further batches land. Do not treat the present count as the

year's total.

**The same cap that distorts 2009 distorts the first half of this year, and

less visibly.** The walk was month-bounded and capped at ten results per query,

so February, April, May and June survive mainly as end-of-month clusters —

26 February to 28 February, 26 to 30 April, 28 to 31 May, 20 to 30 June — while

March, September, October and December run day to day. **No claim about posting

volume, cadence, or a subject going quiet is supportable from the shape of this

page.** Presence is evidence; absence is not.

One consequence worth stating plainly: the year's most important date,

17 February, sits inside a sparse stretch. Three tweets survive from that day

and there may have been more. Nothing on this page should be read as "he said

little about it" — only as "little of what he said was retrieved."

This page is the text archive. Every original and every quote-tweet with Dan's own text that has been retrieved for the year is below, oldest first. Pure reposts with no @danfrank quote content are omitted.

